# Files excluded from the Docker build context.
#
# The build context is what `docker build` sends to the daemon - anything
# listed here is never seen by COPY in the Dockerfile, so it cannot end up
# in any image layer (even one that's later deleted, since deleted files
# still live in lower layers and can be extracted).
#
# Security-critical exclusions go first: secrets, private keys, anything
# that could leak credentials or internal data if the image were exfiltrated.

# --- Secrets and keys (must never enter the image) ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
.aws/
.ssh/

# --- Terraform working state (must never enter the image) ---
#
# `infra/` IS published - the .tf sources are teaching material for
# terraform.html - so this is a carve-out for the working directories, not for
# infra/ as a whole. Added 2026-08-23 after finding nothing here covered them.
#
# CI never had the problem: actions/checkout produces a clean tree and
# .gitignore already keeps all of this out of git. The exposure is a LOCAL
# build - `docker compose up`, which README documents as the way to run the
# site locally, does `build: .` from the repo root. Anyone who has run
# `terraform init` in infra/ then has ~2.4 GB of provider binaries and five
# terraform.tfstate files in the build context, and `COPY . ` puts them in an
# image layer. State files hold resource attributes in plaintext.
#
# nginx 403s these paths at request time (they sit under a dot directory), but
# that is not the control that matters here - the Dockerfile's own comment
# makes the point that deleted files still live in lower layers and can be
# extracted, and these were not even being deleted.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- Repo metadata and CI ---
.git
.github
.claude
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
.lychee.toml
.yamllint.yml
.trivyignore.yaml

# --- Python build / cache / dev artefacts ---
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv
.ruff_cache
pyproject.toml

# --- Internal tooling and audit reports (not for serving) ---
tools/
seo-audits/
*-report.txt
preview-check.txt
normalize-output.txt

# --- Docs and contributor files ---
README.md
LICENSE
CONTRIBUTING*.md
DEVELOPMENT.md
SECURITY.md
RSS_FEED_README.md

# --- Docker-specific files ---
# Dockerfile and docker-compose.yml are not needed inside the image, but
# the .dockerignore-it-out approach is incompatible with how Docker builds
# Dockerfile-relative - we rely on the Dockerfile's post-COPY `rm` step to
# strip them from the final image instead.
docker-compose.yml

# --- macOS metadata ---
.DS_Store
